30:["$","p","Popular choices include Germany, France, the Netherlands, Sweden, Finland, Ireland, and Denmark, depending on the student’s course, budget, and career goals.",{"children":"Popular choices include Germany, France, the Netherlands, Sweden, Finland, Ireland, and Denmark, depending on the student’s course, budget, and career goals."}]
31:["$","p","That depends on the student’s priorities. For many students, Europe offers a better balance of affordability, academic quality, cultural exposure, and future-focused education.",{"children":"That depends on the student’s priorities. For many students, Europe offers a better balance of affordability, academic quality, cultural exposure, and future-focused education."}]
32:["$","p","Yes, many European universities are known for strong research, innovation, and industry-linked programmes in areas like AI, robotics, engineering, sustainability, and fintech.",{"children":"Yes, many European universities are known for strong research, innovation, and industry-linked programmes in areas like AI, robotics, engineering, sustainability, and fintech."}]
33:["$","p","Students benefit from quality education, lower costs, international exposure, access to multiple countries, diverse classrooms, and programmes aligned with emerging global careers.",{"children":"Students benefit from quality education, lower costs, international exposure, access to multiple countries, diverse classrooms, and programmes aligned with emerging global careers."}]
34:["$","p","Yes, one of Europe’s biggest advantages is its connectivity. Students often have the chance to travel across neighbouring countries and experience different cultures during their studies.",{"children":"Yes, one of Europe’s biggest advantages is its connectivity. Students often have the chance to travel across neighbouring countries and experience different cultures during their studies."}]
35:["$","p","Yes, studying in Europe can help students build international exposure, cross-cultural communication skills, and a broader professional network, which are valuable in global careers.",{"children":"Yes, studying in Europe can help students build international exposure, cross-cultural communication skills, and a broader professional network, which are valuable in global careers."}]
36:["$","p","Students should consider their course, tuition budget, language of instruction, career plans, location preferences, and post-study opportunities before making a decision.",{"children":"Students should consider their course, tuition budget, language of instruction, career plans, location preferences, and post-study opportunities before making a decision."}]
37:["$","ul",null,{"children":[["$","li","Why is Europe becoming a popular study abroad destination?",{"children":"Why is Europe becoming a popular study abroad destination?"}],["$","li","Is studying in Europe affordable for international students?",{"children":"Is studying in Europe affordable for international students?"}],["$","li","Can international students study in Europe in English?",{"children":"Can international students study in Europe in English?"}],["$","li","Which European countries are best for international students?",{"children":"Which European countries are best for international students?"}],["$","li","Is Europe better than the US or UK for studying abroad?",{"children":"Is Europe better than the US or UK for studying abroad?"}],["$","li","Are European universities good for AI, technology, and innovation?",{"children":"Are European universities good for AI, technology, and innovation?"}],["$","li","What are the benefits of studying in Europe?",{"children":"What are the benefits of studying in Europe?"}],["$","li","Can students travel while studying in Europe?",{"children":"Can students travel while studying in Europe?"}],["$","li","Does studying in Europe help with global career opportunities?",{"children":"Does studying in Europe help with global career opportunities?"}],["$","li","How do I choose the right university in Europe?",{"children":"How do I choose the right university in Europe?"}]]}]
